    <h2 class="article-title">Of Fellow Believers</h2>
    <div class="article-body">
        {%- if aoidSecondEdition.on %}
        <p><strong>We believe</strong> <span data-span="s7" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">the body of Christ is larger than any single denomination and older than every division</span>. <span data-span="s18" data-article="A08" data-type="direct" data-named="false">Christ taught His disciples to pray to God as "Our Father which art in heaven."</span> <span data-span="s19" data-article="A08" data-type="direct" data-named="false">He explicitly referred to God as "my Father, and your Father," and taught us that our good works should glorify "your Father which is in heaven."</span> In teaching us to call God our Father, He taught us who we are to one another. We are brothers and sisters who seek God the Father through Christ Jesus, <span data-span="s20" data-article="A08" data-type="direct" data-named="false">who set the clear standard: "By this shall all men know that ye are my disciples, if ye have love one to another."</span></p>
        <p>In this same spirit, <span data-span="s1" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">we receive <span data-span="s2" data-article="A08" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">every soul</span> <span data-span="s3" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">who comes to Jesus Christ</span> as a brother, a sister, a fellow child of the same Father in heaven</span>. <span data-span="s4" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We love them whether they return our love or not</span>. <span data-span="s5" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We honor them whether they honor us or not</span>. <span data-span="s6" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We hold them as family whether or not their tradition recognizes ours, and whether or not ours has treated them rightly</span>. <span data-span="s8" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We are not indifferent to Christian institutions or traditions</span>, but we insist that <span data-span="s9" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">the walls of estrangement that often separate the Lord's people were not built by Him</span>. <span data-span="s10" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="true">We <a href="https://www.wordsofplainness.org/studies/contention-and-the-reach-of-christ/" class="article-companion-link">refuse to defend them</a></span>†.</p>
        <p>It is true that various Christian traditions hold irreconcilable convictions about baptism, priesthood authority, sacraments, revelation, and ecclesiastical authority. However, within the sphere of this interfaith ministry, we still honor one another's sincere devotion to Jesus of Nazareth, THE CHRIST. <span data-span="s11" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We will neither allow nor defend the use of any doctrine or teaching as a weapon against a brother or sister <span data-span="s12" data-article="A08" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">who names His name</span></span>. <span data-span="s13" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We will not return insult for insult, exclusion for exclusion, or suspicion for suspicion</span>.</p>
        <p><span data-span="s14" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We will sit at the table with every soul who has found Christ</span>, and <span data-span="s15" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">we will leave the door open to every soul still searching for Him</span>. But hospitality does not require us to permit hostility. We welcome respectful disagreement while protecting the dignity of every participant‡.</p>
        <p><span data-span="s21" data-article="A08" data-type="direct" data-named="false">Disciples of Jesus Christ value fellowship, believing the Lord's promise that "where two or three are gathered together in my name, there am I in the midst of them." We do not forsake the assembling of ourselves together. We gather to pray, to hear and read the scriptures, to sing psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, and to exhort and strengthen one another.</span> The community we offer is <span data-span="s16" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">the fellowship He purchased with His blood</span>: <span data-span="s17" data-article="A08" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">free, plain, and without price</span>.</p>
        {%- else %}
        <p><span data-span="s1" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false"><strong>We receive</strong> <span data-span="s2" data-article="A08" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">every soul</span> <span data-span="s3" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">who comes to Jesus Christ</span> as brother, as sister, as fellow child of the same Father</span>. <span data-span="s4" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We love them whether they return our love or not</span>. <span data-span="s5" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We honor them whether they honor us or not</span>. <span data-span="s6" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We hold them as family whether or not their tradition recognizes ours, and whether or not ours has treated them rightly</span>. We believe <span data-span="s7" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">the body of Christ is larger than any single denomination and older than every division</span>. <span data-span="s8" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We are not indifferent to Christian institutions or traditions</span>, but we insist that <span data-span="s9" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">the walls that often separate the Lord's people were not built by Him</span>. <span data-span="s10" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="true">We <a href="https://www.wordsofplainness.org/studies/contention-and-the-reach-of-christ/" class="article-companion-link">refuse to defend them</a></span>†. <span data-span="s11" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">Nor will we defend any doctrine or teaching made into a weapon against a brother or sister <span data-span="s12" data-article="A08" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">who names His name</span></span>. <span data-span="s13" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We will not return insult for insult, exclusion for exclusion, or suspicion for suspicion</span>. <span data-span="s14" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">We will sit at the table with every soul who has found Christ</span>, and <span data-span="s15" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">we will leave the door open to every soul still searching for Him</span>. The community we offer is <span data-span="s16" data-article="A08" data-type="concept" data-named="false">the fellowship He purchased with His blood</span> — <span data-span="s17" data-article="A08" data-type="paraphrase" data-named="false">free, plain, and without price</span>.</p>
        {%- endif %}
        <div class="article-rjw">
            <p class="rjw-prompt">Who is the hardest person for you to call family in Christ? What would it cost you to hold the door open to them?</p>
            <textarea class="rjw-textarea" data-rjw-key="rjw-A08" placeholder="Your reflection (optional)" rows="3" aria-label="Reflect on Of Fellow Believers"></textarea>
        </div>
        <p class="article-footnote">† See companion study: <a href="https://www.wordsofplainness.org/studies/contention-and-the-reach-of-christ/" class="article-companion-link"><em>Contention, Gatekeeping, and the Reach of Christ</em></a>.</p>{%- if aoidSecondEdition.on %}
        <p class="article-footnote">‡ How we keep this in our gatherings: the <a href="/community-guidelines/" class="article-companion-link">Fellowship Agreement</a>.</p>
        {%- endif %}
    </div>